From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mm: page_alloc: disable watermark boosting and optimize watermark scale for low-memory routers

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

On 512MB embedded enterprise networking gateways (such as Qualcomm IPQ9574 /
IPQ9554), Linux 6.18 kernel initializes watermark_boost_factor to 15000 (150%).
When high-throughput network interfaces (Wi-Fi 6 160MHz ath11k, 5G USB tethering,
and 2.5G SGMII ports) request order-1 and order-2 compound page allocations for
sk_buff packets under memory fragmentation, boost_watermark() inflates the zone
minimum watermark by over 24MB (reaching 40.9MB).

Because managed RAM is ~442MB and over 380MB is actively utilized, any concurrent
user-space allocation (such as Samba, DuFS, or ttyd) triggers premature
out_of_memory kills even when 25-30MB of clean physical RAM remains available.

This MAXNET memory optimization patch:
1. Sets default watermark_boost_factor to 0, completely preventing watermark
   inflation spikes and guaranteeing that all available memory remains accessible
   to system daemons without premature OOM terminations.
2. Tunes default watermark_scale_factor from 10 (0.1%) to 50 (0.5%), giving kswapd
   smooth background reclaim headroom without stalling user processes.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 mm/page_alloc.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -290,8 +290,14 @@
 
-static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 15000;
-static int watermark_scale_factor = 10;
+/* MAXNET Low-Memory VM Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+ * Disable aggressive watermark boosting on 512MB networking platforms to
+ * prevent premature OOM killing of network daemons, and scale watermark
+ * to 50 (0.5%) for smoother page reclaim headroom without memory exhaustion.
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
+ */
+static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 0;
+static int watermark_scale_factor = 50;
 
 static void __setup_per_zone_wmarks(void)
